WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:10.840
Request from Ichigo... when watching the television, sit a safe distance from the television in a well-lit room.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:09.580
Yes. We want to use hand-made gelato for the food wagon match.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.990
Don't even consider it.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.600
The flavours of the ingredients are plain as day in gelato, be it good or bad.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.600
You can't cover up mistakes, and making truly great gelato is difficult.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:23.430
That's precisely the reason my daughter Emma decided not to take over the shop.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.450
I'm not trying to be mean here.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.750
Do something else.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.730
But we really want to challenge gelato!

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.840
We've already gathered ingredients from the marketplace, and chosen the very best.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.930
Landlady, please...

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.040
H-Hey, what do you think you're doing?

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.280
Don't sit down on this dirty floor!

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.880
It's called dogeza.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.860
In Japan, this is how you ask someone for something from the bottom of your heart.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.660
Please!

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.430
OP sequence

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.270
Fine then.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:02.350
But I have two conditions.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.120
First, you have to clean up this dusty old shop.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:07.920
Leave that to us!

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.310
We'll clean it up real good!

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:15.260
And the second is to promise me that you'll make gelato that'll knock my socks off.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.250
You'll see! Just you wait!

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.100
In that case, I'll leave the key to the shop with you.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.020
I'm looking forward to some delicious gelato!

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:28.630
Wow!

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.030
She's even letting us use her kitchen!

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.920
Here we can make sweets just like the pros!

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.950
But cleaning comes first.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.860
I think I'll pass on that.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.150
Oh no you don't!

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:51.160
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:51.160
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:56.530
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:56.530
I'll give you happiness, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:02.030
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, hapinesu made go!

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:02.030
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, Happiness made go!

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:07.210
chansu no tobira aketa toki kara kibun joujou ↑ ↑

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:07.210
Since I opened the door of chance, my mood lifted.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.170
youkoso suiitsu no oukoku he

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.170
Welcome to the Kingdom of Sweets.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.080
Bon appétit!

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:19.430
hajimehane, hetappi demo megezu ni hibishoujin<i>!</i>

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:19.430
Though I was terrible at the beginning, I was diligent everyday<i>!</i>

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.100
「makeruna<i>! atashi」</i>

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.100
「I won't lose<i>!</i> I said to myself」

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.100
Courage!

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:29.880
My dream migakeba hikaru takaramono

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:29.880
My dream when polished is a shining treasure.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.610
fairy chikara kashite<i>!</i>

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.610
Fairy, lend me your strength<i>!</i>

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:37.990
shifon, se shibon, juré, bonjuuru, hatsuratsu furuutsu, raburii made go!

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:37.990
Chiffon, C'est si bon, Gelée, Bonjour, Lively fruits, Lovely made go!

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:44.120
nakitaku natte mo egao ni nareru mahou

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:44.120
Even if you cry, there is magic that can make you smile.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:49.330
「oishii<i>!」 wo tsukurutte omoikkiri tanoshii ne</i>

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:49.330
「Delicious<i>!</i>」 and making it wholeheartedly is fun.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:55.340
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:55.340
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:03:00.680
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:02:55.340 --> 00:03:00.680
I'll give happiness to you, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:05.220
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, fun fun

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:05.220
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, fun, fun

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.430
yume ni eeru<i>!</i>

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.430
Get them in our dreams<i>!</i>

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.940
Presented by Wasurenai-subs

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:18.180
Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.360
Ah, I can't wait~

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:42.180
recipe 42

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:42.180
Gelato of Happiness

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.490
It's all clean...

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.320
Okay, let's get right to work!

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.000
By the way, Ichigo-chan...

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.750
Have you ever made gelato before?

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.460
I've made shaved ice!

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.900
That's like, totally different.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.920
Well, we three can try making the gelato for now.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:08.250
We've done vanilla, chocolate, and strawberry during first year cooking practice,

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.310
but we should perfect some other flavours for now.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.520
I'll try using these French peaches, pêche de vigne.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.110
I'll do pistache.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.320
And I'll do rum raisin.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:41.040
Wow, I can barely recognise the place.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.270
So, are things coming along?

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.780
Yes, splendidly!

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.620
Please wait in the shop!

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:52.510
pêche de vigne.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.010
You used some that weren't ripe, didn't you?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.770
You have to use only ones that are fully ripe.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.360
Otherwise it won't taste good.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.200
I'm sorry...

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.200
Pistache.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.300
You used pistache paste sold at the market, yes?

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.480
That will make the flavour only so-so.

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:22.210
You need to make the pistache paste yourself, from scratch.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.600
R-Right...

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:25.880
Rum raisin.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:32.970
The taste of the rum raisin isn't bad, but the raisins are too hard.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.310
You'd be left with just the taste of raisin.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.120
This won't do.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:45.260
It's not terrible, but you'll never win like this.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:50.240
We've no time to be depressed! Let's hurry and get our revenge!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.330
Okay!

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.220
Oh yes...

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.800
Considering the nature of gelato, you'd need to know how to easily handle large quantities.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:00.630
If you're not busy, why don't you make the cones?

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:02.900
Cones?

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.350
They should be about done.

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:23.900
Right.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.380
Wow, handmade cones!

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.420
Wrap them up right after they finish cooking.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:34.560
Start cooking the next batch right after that.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:39.790
Yeah... When you're stocking, you have to repeat this thirty times.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.670
Thirty times!?

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.850
Annoying, right?

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:47.320
Cooking and wrapping each one can get quite monotonous.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:48.770
That's not true!

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:52.980
Making a ton of delicious cones by yourself is wonderful!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.970
Okay, I'm gonna make a bunch!

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.260
Oww!

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.190
You have to wear gloves!

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.250
How about this?

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.850
Better than the last time, but you still have a long way to go.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:26.340
Okay, one more time!

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:26.960
Right!

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:34.980
Okay, I'll try changing the texture this time.

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.970
If I coarsely chop the pistaches...

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.680
Usually, heating the fruit would deepen the flavour.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:44.200
If I boil this pêche de vigne...

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.700
I'll try making a jam from it.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.990
If I crush the raisins and soak them in rum, they should soften.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.620
How about that?

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:10.840
How is it?

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:13.840
Delicious.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:20.940
All right! She said they were delicious!

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.200
Excellent work.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.270
To be able to improve this much in such a short time...

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:28.190
I can see why you were chosen as a team representing Japan.

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:29.860
But...

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:38.830
These are quite delicious, but they aren't going to win you any competitions.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:43.120
You need another, unique flavour.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.120
Unique flavour?

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.060
Yes.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:49.460
An original flavour that only you can create.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.560
A unique flavour, huh?

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.370
We can't get any more ingredients at this hour.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:58.650
We'll have to make do with what we have here.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:02.060
Hey, do you think these will be of any help?

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:04.440
I brought them from Japan.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.750
Ingredients for Japanese sweets?

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:06.230
Refined Rice Flour

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:10.650
Those could definitely give us an idea for an original flavour...

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.990
Are these sakura?

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:14.790
Yup, sakura.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.410
They've been pickled in salt water.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.950
I wonder what gelato made with these sakura would taste like?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:23.410
Sea-salt ice cream is pretty delicious, you know?

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:29.790
Now that you mention it, they make sweets in France using roses, violets, and pansies, right?

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.620
I think sakura would work well.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:35.940
We also have some Sicilian salt that we bought at the market.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:38.090
Let's try making salt gelato!

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:55.130
It's way too salty!

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.530
And there's no body to it...

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.960
What's the salinity of Yumezuki's salt daifuku?

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.120
About 1%.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.660
Okay, then let's try that next.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:09.860
Now that you mention it, we use honey to help bring out the full flavour of the ingredients.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:12.540
Honey? That might work.

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:18.180
Knowing the perfect balance of sweetness and saltiness will open the door to victory.

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:26.180
Ichigo-chan, want to taste it?

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.230
Sure thing, I'd be happy to!

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:34.720
Delicious!

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:40.480
The harmony between the hearty vanilla gelato and the Sicilian salt...

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:48.310
And the sakura petals blowing through my mouth like a gentle spring breeze...

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:50.290
It's pure bliss!

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:55.330
It's so delicious!

00:10:55.330 --> 00:11:00.720
I'm sure that this gelato will make people so happy that even the landlady would have to admire it!

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:14.610
The Napoleon Courtyard at the Louvre...

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.030
I see. So this is where we battle.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:21.250
Ichigo-senpai, we're definitely not going to lose today!

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.780
You'd better be ready!

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:28.210
When this is over, let's walk back together, just the two of us, <i>Ichigo</i>.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:34.210
Please do not be surprised by the talents of <i>Team</i> Ichigo.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.350
We're not holding back one bit.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:37.990
So, no hard feelings.

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:39.260
Same for us.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:07.820
Everyone, are you all ready?

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:08.410
Yup!

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.850
It's our turn now!

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:13.610
Right! Let's put on the finishing touches.

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.420
Prettyennu Change!

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.450
Deco-deco-decoration!

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:25.930
Just like that!

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:28.770
Prettyennu Change!

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.260
Make up!

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.440
Wow! So cute!

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:40.460
Don't you think this is a little too flashy?

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.840
But we want to stand out, that's the point.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:47.450
You did this on purpose!?

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:50.210
We will go as well.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:51.990
Prettyennu Change!

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:53.730
Deco-deco-decoration!

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:01.310
How cute!

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:04.620
I think we might stand out even more than Ichigo-senpai's cart!

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.300
With this we should be able to attract a lot of girls.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.870
I smell a wonderful honey aroma.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:19.300
That's Tennouji-san's honey waffles!

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:21.320
The French Beauty Brigade is doing crêpes!

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:25.090
The German team is making rarely seen Schneeballs!

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:27.740
The team from Spain is frying up fresh churros.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:31.280
The Portugese team is making egg tarts.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:34.000
Ojou is doing salad de fruits!

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:39.380
And our opponent, Rick, is making piping fresh ring doughnuts!

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:41.570
They all look so...

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:42.880
...delicious!

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.380
We're still preparing!

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:49.390
Please get in line, and wait a little while longer!

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.970
Wow, they already have a line.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.980
Rick's doughnuts and the crêpes have lines, too...

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:01.100
Everyone wants to have a little snack before entering the museum.

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:05.490
I'm kind of getting a chill here.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:10.640
In Paris the temperature can fluctuate so much it feels like summer and winter in a single day.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:14.910
It's especially chilly here, which is in the shade of buildings during the morning.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:17.330
It's already time to start selling...

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:21.070
With it being this cold, no one will...

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.210
Ooh, gelato!

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.060
We've got a lot of yummy gelato for you!

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.100
How about some chocolate?

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.480
We recommend the sakura salt flavour!

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:32.800
It looks great!

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.410
Mama, buy me some gelato!

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:36.450
No, no...

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.930
If you eat gelato your stomach will get chilled.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.650
I couldn't sell it...

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.750
Wow, look at the cute doughnuts!

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.090
Welcome!

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.960
These are American style, ring doughnuts!

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.740
I think they'll be perfect for you cute Parisians!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:57.310
Oh, what a hunk!

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.030
We'd like doughnuts, please!

00:14:59.030 --> 00:14:59.990
Grazie!

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:04.080
As expected by Rick. From the Garçons to the Madames, he's got the perfect pitch!

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.450
I'd like a doughnut, please!

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:07.050
Coming!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.880
Things are selling as expected.

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:09.970
It looks like we're in the game.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.470
Here.

00:15:12.650 --> 00:15:13.740
Merci.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:20.920
Pardon me... What is the honey you used for these waffles?

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:23.750
Marronnier honey.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.380
I see!

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:28.990
I've never had a waffle this delicious even in Belgium itself!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:35.430
The outside is crispy, the inside is fluffy, and above all the aroma of honey is exquisite!

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:38.050
It's truly a work of art!

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:39.700
Thank you very much.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.460
It's cold!

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:49.400
When it's this cold nobody will give a second look at this salad de fruits made from the best, hand-picked fruits!

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:54.970
Since you're so handsome, how about you go draw 'in some customers like that Italian playboy?

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.300
U-Us? We're shy, so we couldn't...

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:00.450
You guys are so useless.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.380
Fine then. In that case...

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:04.980
Yes, Ojou-sama?

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:09.400
Satou, call up the Paris branch of Château confectionery.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.240
Shiotani, you call the factory.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.920
As you wish, Ojou-sama!

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:14.240
Thank you very much!

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:17.810
What's the matter?

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:20.700
No one has bought the sakura gelato yet.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.670
I wonder why?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:29.030
I want a lot of people to get to eat this sakura gelato.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:31.560
But how should I...

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:35.680
I know!

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:39.720
What are you going to do?

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:45.100
Finished!

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:48.020
Everyone!

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:51.760
This is <i>The Da Vinci Code</i> gelato you can only buy here!

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:54.360
Get a souvenir of your visit to the Louvre!

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:58.650
Prettyennu Change!

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:00.900
Deco-deco-decoration!

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.860
The Da Vinci Code gelato?

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:03.870
That sounds interesting.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:08.950
Hey, let's all take a picture of us with The Da Vinci Code gelato!

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:10.400
Yeah!

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:11.740
Let's go!

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:15.430
The end of the line for The Da Vinci Code gelato is back here!

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:18.250
It's hot!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.850
The sun is finally out...

00:17:21.320 --> 00:17:22.430
That's right. Please have a look.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:26.080
Ichigo, not bad.

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:28.440
Ichigo-senpai's finally found her groove, it seems.

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:37.450
Amano-san, go with Kashino and get another batch of the sakura gelato!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.900
Okay!

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:52.500
A Château confectionery bus?

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.250
A company field trip?

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:57.430
They've obviously come to buy Ojou's salad de fruits.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:02.760
Geez! Make them faster, would you?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:09.410
We'll show them at the same time. Got it, Mint-chan?

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:12.030
Fine by me, Vanilla-senpai!

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.500
Then, here we go!

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.610
What? We're tied?

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:23.430
Gelato comes from my home country of Italy.

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:27.100
I wish I could have tried some of Ichigo's The Da Vinci Code gelato...

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.460
Then why don't you go buy one?

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:31.260
Not a chance.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:33.610
This is going to be close... We can't afford to give them even one sale.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:38.120
Don't worry. As the sun sets our team will pull ahead.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:42.450
The tired patrons exiting the museum will want sweet dougnuts.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:46.600
But with weather getting so cold, their gelato won't sell.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.540
It doesn't look like that to me.

00:18:49.570 --> 00:18:50.820
Take a look.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:54.340
All the people exiting have their outerwear in their hands.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:57.140
The inside of the museum must be very hot.

00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:58.860
It seems the gelato will still sell plenty.

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:03.000
Rather than analyzing sales history to find what kind of sweets will be a big hit,

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:06.000
they make sweets that touch people's hearts.

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:10.460
Isn't that the mark of a true pâtissier?

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:16.180
That's the signal for five minutes to go!

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.440
We're almost out of customers.

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:20.200
Maybe we should start cleaning up a bit.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:23.700
Still open?

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:26.050
The landlady!

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:28.050
This is my daughter, Emma.

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:30.860
Sorry we came this late.

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:33.900
How do you do? My mother invited me.

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:36.800
Thanks so much for coming!

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:39.850
So, did you come up with a unique gelato?

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:41.680
Yes! We're quite proud of it.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:44.200
Oh? Then we'll take two.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:48.820
A salt gelato?

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:51.410
What's the accent you've added to it?

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.320
It's sakura.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.900
We used sakura pickled in salt water.

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:57.250
Sakura?

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:01.250
Papa did love sakura flowers...

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:03.240
Yes, I remember.

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:06.480
But to put sakura into it...

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:10.210
That's the finishing signal!

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.230
We will now announce the results.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:21.740
Team Simon
German branch
Team Koshiro
Principality of Andorra branch

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.240
Team Simon vs. Team Koshiro:

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.740
Team Koshiro wins.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:29.240
Team Ricardo
France branch
Team Ichigo
Japan branch

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:25.850
Team Ricardo vs. Team Ichigo:

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:29.240
Team Ichigo wins.

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:31.600
All right!

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:33.790
I'm sure glad the landlady came...

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:42.510
Team                       Angela
Spain branch
Team Tennouji
Japan branch

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.550
Team Angela vs. Team Tennouji:

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:42.510
Team Tennouji wins.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.130
661?

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:47.500
That's almost double what we sold...

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:53.560
Team                      François
France branch
Team Gomez
Portugal branch

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.840
Team François vs. Team Gomez:

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:53.560
Team François wins.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:56.900
Amazing! They scored as high as Tennouji-san's team!

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:02.570
These four teams are the semifinalists.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.840
Congratulations.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.320
Please keep up the good work.

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:15.330
Our victory today is thanks to each customer who bought our gelato.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:18.770
Thank you, everyone!

